## WHY THE FIVE STORED VALUES ARE NOT TOUCHED (the ruling) AND WHAT "UNREAD" MEANS HERE
After this change no code reads `agent_response_style`, `agent_language`, `agent_use_emojis`, `agent_use_markdown` or `agent_role`, and no code writes them. They remain in each deployment's `settings.json` and its backup copies. That is the ruling. Therefore: no migration, no cleanup on boot, no `setSetting`/delete of these keys anywhere, no edit of `backend/jsonStorage.js`, `simpleDb.js` or any defaults list, no change to how settings are exported or backed up. Your new test seeds the five keys in a scratch data directory and holds that they are still there afterwards (cell S1).

